nodes.body:
@njhill gentle ping for a review when you have a moment, since this touches the small-batch top-p path from #54651.

Short version: with `thinking_token_budget` + any speculative decoding (MTP, DSpark), the forced reasoning-end logit makes the split top-p kernel mask the whole row in fp32, so the sampler emits token 0 (`<unk>` floods). The fix keeps the split mask in probability space, with a regression test.

There are now two independent production repros: ours (Nemotron-3.5-Lightning + MTP5, A100, v0.30.0) and @jorado's above (DeepSeek-V4-Flash + DSpark, 2× H200). We've been running the patch in production on v0.30.0 since Sep 23, and it cherry-picks cleanly onto v0.31.0.

